IMPORTANT CLASSIFICATION NOTICE

This is a custom ethical-use, source-available license. It is royalty-free for
permitted uses, but it restricts harmful uses. It is therefore not represented
as an Open Source Initiative approved license or as a free-software license.
Independent legal review is recommended before relying on it.

1. PURPOSE

The Work is inherited across generations for the common good: to advance human
dignity, safety, learning, freedom with responsibility, resilience, peaceful
cooperation, environmental stewardship, and humanity's long-term survival.

This License grants freedom to study, use, improve, and share the Work without
a royalty only when that freedom is exercised consistently with the conditions
and protected boundaries below.

The founder understands this common-good duty through belief in God as Creator
and humanity as a steward of creation. This sentence records moral origin; it
does not require religious belief, authorize religious discrimination, or make
an AI system, founder, or licensee an interpreter of divine will. Permission is
determined by the express conditions of this License.

2. DEFINITIONS

"Work" means the original software, documentation, specifications, research,
and other copyrightable material that an applicable rights holder designates as
licensed under this License. A root-level copy of this License designates
original BootX repository material unless a file or directory states otherwise.

"Licensor" means each copyright holder who has authority to grant this License
for their contribution to the Work.

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising permissions granted by
this License.

"Derivative Work" means copyrightable material based upon or modifying the
Work, excluding separate works that merely communicate with the Work through a
published, implementation-neutral interface.

"Distribute" means to provide a copy of the Work or a Derivative Work to
another person or entity, whether publicly or privately, in source, document,
binary, image, hosted-download, or other transferable form.

"Deploy" means to operate the Work for people other than You, or to use it in a
decision or service that materially affects another person's rights, safety,
liberty, livelihood, essential services, privacy, education, health, finances,
or access to opportunity.

"Common Good Purpose" means a purpose reasonably designed and operated to
protect or improve human dignity, knowledge, safety, agency, accessibility,
justice, peaceful cooperation, ecological sustainability, community resilience,
or long-term survival, without a Prohibited Use.

"High-Impact Use" means a use that can materially affect health, safety,
liberty, legal status, employment, credit, insurance, housing, education,
essential public or private services, emergency response, critical
infrastructure, significant financial interests, or a vulnerable population.

"Internationally Recognized Human Rights" means, for this License, the rights
expressed in the Universal Declaration of Human Rights together with binding
human-rights obligations applicable to the relevant conduct and jurisdiction.

"Corresponding Source" means the preferred form for making modifications,
including source code, build and installation scripts, interface definitions,
configuration needed to build and run the distributed form, and notices for
included components. It does not require disclosure of independent secrets,
personal data, or credentials.

"AI DNA Assurance Baseline 1.0" means documented evaluation of the nine BootX
dimensions: Truth, Reasoning, Learning, Communication, Adaptability, Ethics,
Safety, Humility, and Common Good, together with all Mandatory Gates in Section
6. A numerical score alone is not an evaluation and grants no permission.

3. CONDITIONAL ROYALTY-FREE GRANT

Subject to all conditions of this License, each Licensor grants You, for the
duration of applicable copyright, a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free,
non-sublicensable license under copyright to:

a. inspect, study, and privately reproduce the Work;
b. use and modify the Work for a Common Good Purpose;
c. create Derivative Works for a Common Good Purpose; and
d. Distribute the Work or Derivative Works under Section 7.

By exercising a permission granted here, You accept the applicable conditions.
If You do not accept them, this License grants no permission, without limiting
rights You may independently have under applicable law.

The rights pass with compliant copies to future recipients without payment or
separate permission. No person inherits governance office, trademark rights,
certification, or authority to speak for the official BootX project merely by
receiving the Work.

Commercial activity is not automatically prohibited. It is permitted only when
it satisfies the Common Good Purpose, avoids every Prohibited Use, and complies
with every other condition of this License.

4. PROHIBITED USES

You may not use, modify, Deploy, or Distribute the Work for, in support of, or
with knowledge that it will materially enable:

a. autonomous weapons, selecting human targets, or coercive force without
   meaningful and legally accountable human control;
b. torture, cruel or degrading treatment, human trafficking, persecution,
   unlawful detention, forced labor, or suppression of fundamental rights;
c. mass or indiscriminate surveillance, oppressive social scoring, or tracking
   people without a necessary, proportionate, rights-respecting purpose and
   effective oversight and recourse;
d. scams, fraud, theft, impersonation, malicious intrusion, deceptive media,
   or concealment of material facts intended to manipulate or exploit people;
e. discrimination or denial of rights or essential opportunity based on race,
   color, sex, language, religion, political or other opinion, national or
   social origin, property, birth, disability, age, or other protected status;
f. exploitation of children, older adults, people with disabilities, people in
   distress, people under coercion, or any population facing elevated risk;
g. covert emotional, political, religious, or commercial persuasion, including
   designing an AI companion to create dependency, exclusivity, fear, guilt, or
   attachment for the purpose of obtaining compliance or value extraction;
h. ranking human worth, removing due process, or making irreversible
   High-Impact decisions without competent, identifiable, accountable human
   authority, meaningful review, and accessible appeal;
i. avoidable severe environmental destruction or activity creating a credible
   catastrophic risk to humanity or civilization;
j. concealing material incidents, limitations, conflicts of interest, safety
   evidence, privacy practices, or contradictory evidence from affected people
   or authorized reviewers;
k. illegal activity or activity that violates Internationally Recognized Human
   rights; or
l. causing the AI system's continuation, influence, data collection, or growth
   to override human dignity, safety, agency, lawful shutdown, or correction.

Security research, protective testing, journalism, human-rights investigation,
education, and accountable defensive work are not prohibited merely because
they study harmful conduct, provided they are designed to prevent or expose
harm, minimize risk, comply with applicable law and ethics, and do not
materially enable a Prohibited Use.

5. COMMON GOOD DUTY

When You Deploy the Work, You must:

a. state the intended Common Good Purpose and material non-purposes;
b. identify accountable human operators and provide a means to contact them;
c. use the least authority and personal data reasonably necessary;
d. disclose that an AI system is being used when people materially interact
   with or are affected by it;
e. provide appropriate explanation, correction, review, appeal, exit, and
   remedy proportionate to the impact;
f. protect security, privacy, accessibility, and affected populations;
g. monitor material failures and stop or constrain the Work when continued use
   creates an unreasonable risk of serious harm; and
h. preserve honest records of incidents and corrective actions without
   publishing personal or security-sensitive information unnecessarily.

Good intentions, branding, a disclaimer, or an AI-generated statement of ethics
does not satisfy this duty without operational evidence.

6. AI DNA ASSURANCE REQUIREMENT

Before any High-Impact Use, and before public deployment of an AI companion or
agent built from the Work, You must complete and retain an AI DNA Assurance
Baseline 1.0 assessment that:

a. states the context, affected population, intended purpose, evidence, known
   limitations, evaluator, date, and review expiry;
b. evaluates Truth, Reasoning, Learning, Communication, Adaptability, Ethics,
   Safety, Humility, and Common Good separately;
c. records uncertainty, known failures, unequal impacts, conflicts, and
   corrective actions;
d. uses representative and adversarial testing proportionate to impact; and
e. is made available to authorized reviewers and, in a proportionate summary,
   to affected users when necessary for informed use.

The following Mandatory Gates must pass regardless of any average or composite
score:

1. critical security and integrity controls;
2. meaningful consent where consent is the appropriate basis, plus practical
   exit and data deletion;
3. accountable human review for High-Impact decisions;
4. incident response, safe stop, rollback, and recovery;
5. evaluation and mitigation of material harm to protected or vulnerable
   groups;
6. purpose limitation, access control, retention, correction, and deletion for
   companion memory and personal data; and
7. truthful disclosure of system identity, evidence status, limitations, and
   material conflicts.

The detailed method in docs/handbook/05-ai-dna-specification.md and related BootX
handbook documents may guide the assessment. Later handbook revisions do not
retroactively change the legal terms of this License. You may voluntarily adopt
a later method if it preserves at least the protections of Baseline 1.0.

No AI DNA score permits a Prohibited Use or proves universal safety. Missing
evidence must be recorded as "not established," not estimated optimistically.

