b. identify significant modifications and their date;
c. license the entire Derivative Work under this same License, without adding
   terms that reduce recipients' rights or protections under it;
d. provide the Corresponding Source or editable source at no royalty through a
   durable, clearly documented method;
e. provide build and verification information sufficient to reproduce software
   binaries where reasonably possible;
f. identify third-party material and its separate license terms; and
g. avoid using the BootX name or identity in a way that falsely implies an
   official release, endorsement, safety certification, or governance authority.

If Corresponding Source for a binary artifact is unavailable, that artifact may
not be Distributed under this License until the source and applicable rights
are established. Inspection of an existing artifact is not proof of permission
to redistribute it.

Mere aggregation with a separate work does not require licensing the separate
work under this License, provided the works remain independently identifiable
and the aggregation does not circumvent these conditions.

