10. NOTICE, CURE, AND TERMINATION

Your rights terminate automatically when You materially violate this License.

For a violation not involving a deliberate Prohibited Use, rights are
reinstated provisionally if You stop the violation promptly after discovery and
permanently if You cure it within 30 days after receiving written notice from a
Licensor, unless the Licensor states a reasonable unresolved remediation need.

For a deliberate Prohibited Use, rights remain terminated unless and until the
applicable Licensor confirms in writing that the use has ceased and reasonable
remediation has occurred. Termination does not remove obligations to protect
affected people, preserve evidence, provide remedy, delete data when required,
or comply with law.

Only a rights holder or authorized party can enforce copyright terms. Project
governance review, community concern, or an AI DNA assessment does not by itself
adjudicate legal liability.

